---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import Main from "@/components/Main.astro";
import config, { analytics } from "@/config";

const enabled = import.meta.env.PROD && analytics;
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy | ${config.site.title}`}
  description="How this website handles optional analytics and your privacy choices."
>
  <Header />
  <Main pageTitle="Privacy" class="app-prose">
    <p>
      This is {config.site.author}'s personal writing website, hosted on GitHub
      Pages. GitHub processes requests to serve the website under its
      <a
        href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        >privacy statement</a
      >.
    </p>
    <h2 id="analytics">Optional analytics</h2>
    <p data-analytics-state>
      {
        enabled
          ? "Optional Google Analytics is available on the published website, but stays off unless you accept."
          : "Google Analytics is not enabled in this version of the website."
      }
    </p>
    <p>
      When enabled and accepted, Google Analytics 4 helps me understand which
      pages attract readers, where visits come from, and which article and
      external links readers select. Google receives page and event information,
      including page titles, sanitized URLs and referrers, article identifiers,
      link destinations, and campaign labels. Analytics can also report
      engagement time and browser, device, and approximate location information.
    </p>
    <p>
      Accepting analytics allows Google Analytics to use first-party cookies
      such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_...</code> to distinguish browsers and
      sessions. These identifiers do not tell me your name. No advertising personalization,
      Google Signals, account identity tracking, or session recordings are enabled
      by this integration.
    </p>
    <p>
      The website does not intentionally send raw site-search terms to
      Analytics. Unneeded URL query parameters and fragments are removed from
      the page and link information sent by the integration. Please do not put
      personal information in campaign parameters.
    </p>
    <p>
      No Google Analytics script, analytics cookies, or analytics requests are
      initiated until you accept. Rejecting analytics does not limit access to
      any articles or website features.
    </p>
    <h2>Changing your choice</h2>
    <p>
      When analytics is available, use the footer's Analytics preferences
      control to accept or reject analytics later. Your explicit choice is
      stored in your browser's local storage under <code>analytics-consent</code
      >. If the consent policy materially changes, you will be asked again.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="#analytics" data-analytics-preferences hidden
        >Change analytics preferences</a
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      Withdrawing consent stops new analytics collection, removes accessible
      Google Analytics cookies for this website, and reloads the page without
      the tracker. Withdrawal does not erase information already sent to Google.
      Clearing your website storage also removes your saved preference.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google processes analytics data under its
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>. Read
      <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245"
        >Google's information on safeguarding Analytics data</a
      > for more detail.
    </p>
    <h2>Other local storage and search</h2>
    <p>
      The website stores your color-theme preference locally. Session storage
      remembers navigation context for the back button. These preferences are
      separate from analytics consent. Site search uses a downloaded Pagefind
      index in your browser rather than sending your search terms to Google.
    </p>
    <h2>Google Search Console</h2>
    <p>
      Search Console provides aggregate reports about this website's appearance
      in Google Search. It does not require an Analytics tracker on this website
      and does not tell me which named person visited an article.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about this website, contact me through
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/erdem-tuna/">LinkedIn</a>.
    </p>
  </Main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
